                                            BUSINESS QUESTIONS
Which stocks recorded the highest growth over time?

                          Query                                          
    SELECT DISTINCT
    name,
    FIRST_VALUE(close) OVER(
                             PARTITION BY name 
                             ORDER BY date) AS starting_price,
    LAST_VALUE(close) OVER(
                           PARTITION BY name 
                            ORDER BY date ROWS BETWEEN
                            UNBOUNDED PRECEDING AND UNBOUNDED FOLLOWING 
                            ) AS ending_price,
    ROUND(
        ( LAST_VALUE(close) OVER(
                                PARTITION BY name ORDER BY date 
                             ROWS BETWEEN UNBOUNDED PRECEDING AND UNBOUNDED FOLLOWING
                    )
            -
            FIRST_VALUE(close) OVER(PARTITION BY name ORDER BY date
            )
        )
        /
        FIRST_VALUE(close) OVER(
            PARTITION BY name
            ORDER BY date
        ) * 100,
    2) AS growth_percentage
FROM stock_data
ORDER BY growth_percentage DESC;


Insight:
The result shows the stocks with the strongest long term growth based on their starting and ending prices. Stocks with higher growth percentages
indicate stronger long-term investment performance and better market appreciation over time.


Recommendation:
The company should focus more on stocks with consistent long-term growth patterns, as they may provide better investment opportunities and stronger
future returns.

